    ['Fathom', 'Fathom\u2019s free recorder is good. Pacenote\u2019s is free too and never leaves your Mac: transcript, screen, notes. Plus the part Fathom skips: your files before the call and answers during it. If your team shares recordings in Fathom, keep it for that.'],
    ['Granola', 'Pacenote writes the notes after the call too, and the audio is transcribed on your Mac. The difference is before and during: a brief from your project files, and the number, date or sentence you need under your camera while you talk.'],
    ['Zoom, Teams, Meet AI', 'Built-in AI lives in one platform. Pacenote works the same in Zoom, Meet, Teams and Slack, knows your project, and helps during the call. From Google Meet it imports the participants and the Meet transcript.'],
    ['Just notes', 'Keep writing if you like. Pacenote reads your doc before the call, along with Notion, Google Docs and earlier calls, shows the line you need during the call, and writes the notes to Notion, Google Docs, Word or Markdown after it.'],
